OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,382,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38102
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F381A1786022313
OL,3,CGreat Train Robbery mailbag signed by
OL,4,C10 gang members up for auction
OL,6,FIn the early hours of 8 August 1963,
OL,7,Fthe gang rigged signals to stop the
OL,8,FTravelling Post Office train at
OL,9,FBridego Railway Bridge near Ledburn in
OL,10,FBuckinghamshire, escaping with #2.6
OL,11,Fmillion in used banknotes - worth over
OL,12,F#50 million today.
OL,14,FThe item bears the signatures of the
OL,15,Fheist's most infamous figures,
OL,16,Fincluding mastermind Bruce Reynolds,
OL,17,Fgetaway driver Roy James, and Ronnie
OL,18,FBiggs.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G2/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,382,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38103
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F381A1786022313
OL,3,CGreat Train Robbery mailbag signed by
OL,4,C10 gang members up for auction
OL,6,FAlso featured is the signature of
OL,7,FBuster Edwards, whose escape to Mexico
OL,8,Fand subsequent life running a flower
OL,9,Fstall inspired the 1988 Phil Collins
OL,10,Ffilm Buster.
OL,12,FOther signatories include Charlie
OL,13,FWilson, Gordon Goody, Roger Cordrey,
OL,14,FBob Welch, Tommy Wisbey, and James
OL,15,FHussey.
OL,17,FAuctioneers have placed an estimate of
OL,18,F#70 to #100 on the signed bag.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G3/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,382,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38104
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F381A1786022313
OL,3,CGreat Train Robbery mailbag signed by
OL,4,C10 gang members up for auction
OL,6,FOffered in a separate lot is an
OL,7,Foriginal Monopoly #500 note directly
OL,8,Flinked to the investigation that
OL,9,Fcracked the case.
OL,11,FFollowing the robbery, the gang fled
OL,12,Fto their safehouse at Leatherslade
OL,13,FFarm, near Oakley and Brill in
OL,14,FBuckinghamshire.
OL,16,FWhile lying low, they famously used
OL,17,Freal stolen cash alongside play money
OL,18,Fto play games of Monopoly.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G4/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,382,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38105
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F381A1786022313
OL,3,CGreat Train Robbery mailbag signed by
OL,4,C10 gang members up for auction
OL,6,FWhen police raided the farm, forensic
OL,7,Fteams lifted vital fingerprints from
OL,8,Fthe Monopoly set, ultimately leading
OL,9,Fto the gang's arrest and subsequent
OL,10,Ftrial at Aylesbury Crown Court.
OL,12,FThe lot also includes:
OL,14,FThe Monopoly note and signed
OL,15,Fphotograph collection carries a guide
OL,16,Fprice of #100 to #150. Both items come
OL,17,Ffrom the estate of a dedicated
OL,18,Fmemorabilia collector.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G5/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
